describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1Replies"} → {"operationId":"postV1Replies","method":"POST","path":"/v1/replies","summary":"Reply to a person in their existing email thread","description":"Send an answer into the email thread a person already has with the brand, from the mailbox and persona that wrote to them (the reply a sales rep would send). Name the person by `email` alone: the thread is found from it. When that person wrote back on several campaigns the answer is 409 `ambiguous_thread` with the `candidates`; call again with one `campaign_id`. Write `body_html` without a signature (the persona's is added). Send `sent_by: "human"` for a reply a person decided on. Name the organization with `brandId` or `orgId`. To send files, list offer documents in `attachments` [{ document_id }] (up to 5, 10 MB together; ids from `GET /v1/brands/{id}/offers/{offerId}/documents`): each goes as a real email attachment, and any problem refuses the whole reply, nothing sent (404 `attachment_not_found`, 422 `attachment_too_large` or `attachments_unsupported_on_transport`, 502 `attachment_unavailable`). Pass-through to instantly-service POST /orgs/replies: refusals come back unchanged with a `code` (409 `ambiguous_thread`, `no_reply_to_thread`, `human_took_over`; 404 `campaign_not_found` when the org never emailed that person). The full body is documented from instantly-service.

Request body: documented from instantly-service POST /orgs/replies, which owns and validates it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.

Response: documented from instantly-service POST /orgs/replies, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged. Its full document: GET /v1/platform/services/instantly.","params":[],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"campaign_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Logical campaign id — the same key manual qualifications and opt-outs use. OPTIONAL: omit it and the thread is found from `email` alone. A thread is a campaign of this org in which the prospect wrote back. Exactly one → the reply goes into it. Several → 409 `ambiguous_thread` listing each candidate (`campaign_id` + `last_message_at`); call again naming one. None but we did email them → 409 `no_reply_to_thread`. Never emailed by this org → 404 `campaign_not_found`. When given, it is used as-is."},"email":{"type":"string","format":"email","description":"The prospect who replied. Matched case-insensitively. Enough on its own to find the thread when `campaign_id` is omitted."},"body_html":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The answer, HTML. Signed by this service with the sending account's persona — do NOT include a signature."},"sent_by":{"type":"string","enum":["human","automation"],"description":"Who asked for this answer to be sent. Only an `automation` reply goes through the hand-over and stated-not-to-brand gates; a `human` reply never does. A person's earlier hand reply on the thread never refuses an automated one: it stays in the conversation the responder reads. Absent resolves to `automation`; a human surface declares `human` explicitly."},"attachments":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"document_id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"An offer document id (UUID) from brand-service, of THIS org (x-org-id)."}},"required":["document_id"]},"maxItems":5,"description":"Offer documents to attach to the reply as real files (a case study, a one-pager). This service reads each one from brand-service, bytes included, as this org, and attaches it under brand-service's filename and type. Up to 5, 10 MB together. FAIL LOUD, nothing sent: unknown or another org's document = 404 `attachment_not_found`; over the limits = 422 `attachment_too_large`; brand-service unreadable = 502 `attachment_unavailable`; a thread on the Instantly pipe (no attachment support) = 422 `attachments_unsupported_on_transport`. Absent or empty = the reply exactly as before. Replies only: cold sequence steps never carry a file."}},"required":["email","body_html"],"example":{"campaign_id":"c1a2b3c4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001","email":"alice@media.com","body_html":"<p>Great — how does Thursday 3pm look?</p>","sent_by":"automation"}},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"The reply was sent (instantly-service shape)","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","enum":[true]},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["sent"]},"reply":{"type":"object","properties":{"transport":{"type":"string","enum":["instantly","smtp"],"description":"Which pipe carried the reply — the one that carried the outreach"},"instantlyCampaignId":{"type":"string"},"leadEmail":{"type":"string"},"accountEmail":{"type":"string","description":"The mailbox that answered. Resolved by this service, never supplied by the caller."},"from":{"type":"string","description":"The From header as the prospect sees it, persona included"},"subject":{"type":"string","description":"The conversation's own subject under `Re:`"},"cc":{"type":"string","description":"The agency inbox this reply was CC'd to — VISIBLE to the prospect, so a reply-all reaches a human. Never a BCC."},"messageId":{"type":"string","description":"Instantly's email id, or the RFC 5322 Message-Id we sent"},"inReplyTo":{"type":"string","description":"The prospect message this reply threads onto"},"attachments":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"documentId":{"type":"string","description":"The brand-service offer document id"},"filename":{"type":"string"},"contentType":{"type":"string"},"sizeBytes":{"type":"integer"},"md5":{"type":"string","description":"Hex md5 of the exact bytes attached"}},"required":["documentId","filename","contentType","sizeBytes","md5"]},"description":"The files this reply carried. Absent when it carried none."}},"required":["transport","instantlyCampaignId","leadEmail","accountEmail","from","subject","cc","messageId","inReplyTo"]}},"required":["success","status","reply"]}}],"needsTheirYes":{"why":"Sends a reply to a person in their email thread.","because":["sends_to_person"],"notNeededWhen":[]}}

describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1FollowupCuts"} → {"operationId":"postV1FollowupCuts","method":"POST","path":"/v1/followup-cuts","summary":"Stop the queued follow-ups of named leads a campaign emailed in error","description":"Pass-through to instantly-service POST /orgs/followup-cuts. For leads a campaign should never have written to (a sourcing mistake): the rest of their sequence will not go out. Every other lead of the campaign keeps its follow-ups. Body `{ campaignId, leadEmails[], reason }`. Not an opt-out: nothing is recorded as unsubscribe or suppression. All or nothing on names: an email the campaign never wrote to is a 404 `leads_not_in_campaign` and nothing is cut. Idempotent (`already_cut`). Audited: who, when, why (GET /v1/followup-cuts). A lead that could not be cut answers 502.

